   "body": "Published a fix in my fork: https://github.com/skygunner/magpie/commit/4671590ddd370d6b95ee6800980f46c62f45fe84\n\nThe window assertion now records only that window's requests, separately from the still-open panel. A regression check explicitly makes the panel issue its unfiltered request after the window has sent the correct filtered request. Existing provider/agent filter assertions remain in place; production UI code is unchanged.\n\nThe old shared request array fails with that interleaving. The committed test passes all four cases: Chromium and WebKit, English and Chinese, using Playwright 1.62.1. This fixes the test interference reported here, rather than claiming a production filtering defect.\n\nCombined verification at `4671590ddd370d6b95ee6800980f46c62f45fe84` ([batch branch](https://github.com/skygunner/magpie/tree/fix/issue-batch-20261023-m)): native/Linux/Windows vet and builds, plus the full `go test -tags nogui ./... -count=1 -timeout=45m` suite, all passed with Go 1.26.8 and an isolated HOME. The new Go regressions also pass together with `-race -count=5`. These full checks apply to the combined head, not separate full-suite runs on each ancestor. No upstream PR opened.\n",
