   "body": "Re-derived on `2cdbe92de` — same hunk as 4671590dd, only the offset moved because upstream gained lines above it:\n\n- Branch: https://github.com/skygunner/magpie/tree/fix/3311-panel-request-isolation\n- Commit: `18f05d73e632a269d388d42279c9b39030e23a91`\n- 8 lines in `internal/gui/tests/panel-usage.test.cjs`: the window's usage request gets its own log instead of the shared `asked` one that the live panel's poll also writes to.\n\nWithout it, the assertion at `panel-usage.test.cjs:427` waits on `settled(asked, …)`, so under load the window's `settled` can observe the panel's own `period=today&limit=1` poll instead of the window's request and go red on the wrong request.\n\n`node --test internal/gui/tests/panel-usage.test.cjs` → 4/4 pass. Honest limit: the race is load-dependent and did not reproduce on this host in a plain run; the failure mode was reproduced with a two-page demo that keeps the pre-patch shared log and issues the panel poll late — the window's settled check then matches the panel's request.\n",
   "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
