     "body": "The Left/Used switch flips every subscription window, but a custom provider's balance meter always shows\nthe used share, both its figure and its bar.\n\n**Reproduction**\n\n1. Add a custom provider whose balance endpoint reports a daily allowance as a percent used, e.g. a reply of\n   ```json\n   { \"windows\": [ { \"name\": \"daily\", \"used\": 8.9 } ] }\n   ```\n   with\n   ```\n   magpie provider set <id> balance=<url> \"balance.path=Daily: windows.0.used / 100%\"\n   ```\n2. The provider's card shows `Daily 8.9%` with a bar filled to 8.9%. That is right for **Used**.\n3. Switch the quota display to **Left** (Usage page, or the tray panel's Used/Left button).\n4. Subscription cards now read `… left`. The custom provider's card still reads `Daily 8.9%` with an 8.9% bar.\n\n**Expected:** with Left on, the balance meter reads `91.1% left` and its bar fills to 91.1%, like every other\nwindow.\n\n**Where it happens**\n\n- `internal/provider/balance.go` `balanceAmount` / `balanceShare`: the part's `text` (`\"8.9%\"`) is formatted in\n  Go as the used share. `percent` carries the same number for the bar.\n- `internal/gui/assets/app.js` `panelBalances` (tray panel, `if (p.percent != null) card.append(balanceMeter(p.percent))`)\n  and `balanceRow` (Usage page, same call): neither checks `quotaLeft`. `balanceMeter` fills to `percent` as is.\n- Subscription windows go through `quotaFill` / `quotaText`, which do `quotaLeft ? 100 - used : used` and label\n  `{n} left` / `{n} used`.\n\n**Suggested fix**\n\nFor a balance part that has `percent`, render it the way `quotaText`/`quotaFill` render a window: with Left on,\nshow `100 − percent` and label it `left`, and fill the bar to the same share. Keep the \"nearly full\" colour keyed\nto the used share. A part without `percent` (money, counts) is unchanged. The switch is already stored in\nSettings, so the tray panel, the Usage page and any alert text would follow it the same way.\n",
